# Upstream License Registry

ScreenMint is MIT licensed. This file tracks upstream runtime and asset license
obligations for public beta release artifacts.

## Release Gate

Run `npm run release:validate-provenance` before publishing. The command passes only when
`docs/ASSET_PROVENANCE.md`, `THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md`, and this file contain concrete
asset provenance/status language.

## Verified Project-Owned Assets

- ScreenMint brand source assets in `branding/source-assets/`.
- Generated app and installer icons in `public/app-icons/` and `icons/icons/`.
- Native helper source under `electron/native/`.

## Maintainer-Attested Redistributable Assets

The maintainer confirms that these bundled asset groups are copyright-free or otherwise
approved for redistribution in the public beta and open-source repository:

- MediaPipe Tasks Vision runtime files in `public/mediapipe/`.
- Webcam segmentation model in `public/models/selfie_segmenter_landscape.tflite`.
- `web-demuxer` runtime in `public/wasm/web-demuxer.wasm`.
- Bundled editor wallpapers and generated thumbnails in `public/wallpapers/`.
- App sounds and built-in editor music in `src/assets/audio/`, including Mixkit-named
  files.
- Cursor SVGs and cursor packs in `src/assets/cursors/`.
- Website screenshots, GIFs, and preview images in `website/public/images/`.

New bundled assets require a matching source/status/proof note in
`docs/ASSET_PROVENANCE.md` and `THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md`.

Do not delete bundled assets during provenance cleanup unless the maintainer explicitly
asks for removal.
